{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ArchimedeanMassFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanMassFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.Torsion","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.consistent_with_MassDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.consistent_with_MassDerivation","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L120-L127","doc":"The mass formula is consistent with the `MassDerivation` module:\n`h_q_def` guarantees `h_q = 1 - 1/q`, so we recover exactly\nthe `TopologicalMassFormula` structure from `MassDerivation.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.mass_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.mass_pos","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L112-L118","doc":"The mass is positive (since the knot volume is positive and ℏ_q² > 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.mass_eq_vol_div_h_q_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.mass_eq_vol_div_h_q_sq","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L93-L110","doc":"**Theorem.** Given the two evaluation hypotheses, the total mass\nequals `Vol(K) / ℏ_q²`.\n\nThis is the algebraic consequence of the decomposition identity\n`m = baseline + Σ exceptional` combined with the two evaluations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.h_q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.h_q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L82-L91","doc":"The quantum Planck constant is non-zero when `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.exceptional_sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.exceptional_sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L79-L79","doc":"**Hypothesis 2 (Dilogarithm evaluation).**\nThe sum of exceptional divisor contributions, evaluated in\nBriggs–Klein spectral coordinates, yields\n`Vol(K) · (1/ℏ_q² − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.baseline_eq_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.baseline_eq_volume","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L74-L74","doc":"**Hypothesis 1 (Chern–Simons/Volume correspondence).**\nThe baseline holonomy of the QOU connection evaluates to the\nhyperbolic volume of the knot complement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.knotVolume_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.knotVolume_pos","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The knot volume is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.knotVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.knotVolume","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The hyperbolic volume of the knot `K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.h_q_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.h_q_def","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The quantum Planck constant satisfies its defining equation.\nThis constraint ensures `h_q` cannot be overridden to an\ninconsistent value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.h_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.h_q","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 − 1/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The substrate parameter exceeds classicality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.q","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The substrate parameter `q > 1` at the evaluation point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.toTopologicalMassDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula.toTopologicalMassDecomposition","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L56-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula","kind":"structure","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanMassFormula.lean#L43-L80","doc":"**Proposition (Topological Mass Formula — Archimedean).**\n\nIn the ℂ-quantum observable universe, the mass of a particle\nassociated with a hyperbolic knot K satisfies `m(K) = Vol(K) / ℏ_q²`,\nwhere `Vol(K)` is the hyperbolic volume of `S³ \\ K` and\n`ℏ_q = 1 − 1/q` is the quantum Planck constant.\n\nThis structure extends `TopologicalMassDecomposition` with the two\nevaluation identities (Chern–Simons/volume correspondence and\nBriggs–Klein dilogarithm evaluation) that specialise the general\ndecomposition to the archimedean closed form.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:topological-mass-formula}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:topological-mass-formula","label":"prop:topological-mass-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}